{"headword":"אַהֲבָה","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.f. love (</strong>= Inf. of <span dir=\"rtl\">אהב</span> q.v.<strong>)</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 10:12\" href=\"/Proverbs.10.12\">Pr 10:12</a> + 18 times; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">אַהֲבַת</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 2:2\" href=\"/Jeremiah.2.2\">Je 2:2</a> + 3 times; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אַהֲבָתִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 109:4\" href=\"/Psalms.109.4\">ψ 109:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 109:5\" href=\"/Psalms.109.5\">5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אַהֲבָֽתְךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 1:26\" href=\"/II_Samuel.1.26\">2 S 1:26</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אַהֲבָתוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 63:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.63.9\">Is 63:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 3:17\" href=\"/Zephaniah.3.17\">Zp 3:17</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אַהֲבָתָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:19\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.19\">Pr 5:19</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אַהֲבָתָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 9:6\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.9.6\">Ec 9:6</a>—<em>love</em>, especially WisdLt & late."},{"senses":[{"definition":"human (to human obj.) abs. <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 9:1\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.9.1\">Ec 9:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 9:6\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.9.6\">6</a> (both ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שִׂנְאָה</span>) so <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 10:12\" href=\"/Proverbs.10.12\">Pr 10:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 15:17\" href=\"/Proverbs.15.17\">15:17</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:5\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.5\">27:5</a>; v. also <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:9\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.9\">17:9</a>; of man toward man <a data-ref=\"Psalms 109:4\" href=\"/Psalms.109.4\">ψ 109:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 109:5\" href=\"/Psalms.109.5\">5</a>; love for one’s self <span dir=\"rtl\">(נַפְשׁוֹ)</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.17\">1 S 20:17</a>; between man & woman <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:4\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.4\">Ct 2:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:5\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.5\">5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:8\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.8\">5:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:6\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.6\">8:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:7\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.7\">7</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 5:19\" href=\"/Proverbs.5.19\">Pr 5:19</a> cf. also <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 1:26\" href=\"/II_Samuel.1.26\">2 S 1:26</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(א׳ נָשִׁים)</span>; personif. <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 2:7\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.2.7\">Ct 2:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 3:5\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.3.5\">3:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 7:7\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.7.7\">7:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:4\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.4\">8:4</a>; cf. fig. use <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 3:10\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.3.10\">3:10</a>; of mere sexual desire <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:15\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.15\">2 S 13:15</a>; fig. of Jerusalem’s love to <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 2:2\" href=\"/Jeremiah.2.2\">Je 2:2</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(א׳ כַּלוּלֹתַיִךְ)</span>, & of love of adulter. Jerus. v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 2:33\" href=\"/Jeremiah.2.33\">33</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"God’s love to his people <a data-ref=\"Hosea 11:4\" href=\"/Hosea.11.4\">Ho 11:4</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(עֲבֹתוֹת א׳)</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 31:3\" href=\"/Jeremiah.31.3\">Je 31:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 63:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.63.9\">Is 63:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 3:17\" href=\"/Zephaniah.3.17\">Zp 3:17</a>."}],"num":"2."}]},"rid":"BDB00171","strong_numbers":["160"],"next_hw":"אהד","prev_hw":"אֹ֫הַב","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["173","174"],"TWOT":["29c"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Bro